# GHC artifacts from the sketch
*.hi
*.o

# Rust
server/target/
target/

# .NET
client/bin/
client/obj/
**/bin/
**/obj/

# Data: raw downloads are reproducible via data/fetch-raw.ps1 + atlas-etl and
# stay gitignored; data/compiled/ is the app's actual runtime data and IS
# committed (see README.md's "Data" section and LICENSES.md) so a fresh
# clone runs with zero downloads.
data/raw/*
!data/raw/README.md

# Node / test tooling
node_modules/
tests/ux/test-results/
tests/ux/playwright-report/

# client/wwwroot/vendor/ is COMMITTED on purpose: index.html loads Leaflet
# (BSD-2-Clause, redistributable -- see LICENSES.md) from vendor/leaflet/,
# and a clone that lacks it gets index.html served in leaflet.js's place by
# the SPA fallback ("Unexpected token '<'"), breaking clone-and-run.

# Publish output (dotnet publish client -o publish; see README's publish-path
# section) -- a build artifact, never committed.
publish/
